{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '973,1006p' ../agent-source/raft.go\nsed -n '1185,1233p' ../agent-source/raft.go\nsed -n '275,319p' ../agent-source/log.go\nsed -n '1857,1938p' ../agent-source/raft.go\"","aggregated_output":"func (r *raft) hup(t CampaignType) {\n\tif r.state == StateLeader {\n\t\tr.logger.Debugf(\"%x ignoring MsgHup because already leader\", r.id)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tif !r.promotable() {\n\t\tr.logger.Warningf(\"%x is unpromotable and can not campaign\", r.id)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tif r.hasUnappliedConfChanges() {\n\t\tr.logger.Warningf(\"%x cannot campaign at term %d since there are still pending configuration changes to apply\", r.id, r.Term)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tr.logger.Infof(\"%x is starting a new election at term %d\", r.id, r.Term)\n\tr.campaign(t)\n}\n\n// errBreak is a sentinel error used to break a callback-based loop.\nvar errBreak = errors.New(\"break\")\n\nfunc (r *raft) hasUnappliedConfChanges() bool {\n\tif r.raftLog.applied >= r.raftLog.committed { // in fact applied == committed\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\tfound := false\n\t// Scan all unapplied committed entries to find a config change. Paginate the\n\t// scan, to avoid a potentially unlimited memory spike.\n\tlo, hi := r.raftLog.applied+1, r.raftLog.committed+1\n\t// Reuse the maxApplyingEntsSize limit because it is used for similar purposes\n\t// (limiting the read of unapplied committed entries) when raft sends entries\n\t// via the Ready struct for application.\n\t// TODO(pavelkalinnikov): find a way to budget memory/bandwidth for this scan\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\tr.hup(campaignElection)\n\t\t}\n\n\tcase pb.MsgStorageAppendResp:\n\t\tif m.Index != 0 {\n\t\t\tr.raftLog.stableTo(entryID{term: m.LogTerm, index: m.Index})\n\t\t}\n\t\tif m.Snapshot != nil {\n\t\t\tr.appliedSnap(m.Snapshot)\n\t\t}\n\n\tcase pb.MsgStorageApplyResp:\n\t\tif len(m.Entries) > 0 {\n\t\t\tindex := m.Entries[len(m.Entries)-1].Index\n\t\t\tr.appliedTo(index, entsSize(m.Entries))\n\t\t\tr.reduceUncommittedSize(payloadsSize(m.Entries))\n\t\t}\n\n\tcase pb.MsgVote, pb.MsgPreVote:\n\t\t// We can vote if this is a repeat of a vote we've already cast...\n\t\tcanVote := r.Vote == m.From ||\n\t\t\t// ...we haven't voted and we don't think there's a leader yet in this term...\n\t\t\t(r.Vote == None && r.lead == None) ||\n\t\t\t// ...or this is a PreVote for a future term...\n\t\t\t(m.Type == pb.MsgPreVote && m.Term > r.Term)\n\t\t// ...and we believe the candidate is up to date.\n\t\tlastID := r.raftLog.lastEntryID()\n\t\tcandLastID := entryID{term: m.LogTerm, index: m.Index}\n\t\tif canVote && r.raftLog.isUpToDate(candLastID) {\n\t\t\t// Note: it turns out that that learners must be allowed to cast votes.\n\t\t\t// This seems counter- intuitive but is necessary in the situation in which\n\t\t\t// a learner has been promoted (i.e. is now a voter) but has not learned\n\t\t\t// about this yet.\n\t\t\t// For example, consider a group in which id=1 is a learner and id=2 and\n\t\t\t// id=3 are voters. A configuration change promoting 1 can be committed on\n\t\t\t// the quorum `{2,3}` without the config change being appended to the\n\t\t\t// learner's log. If the leader (say 2) fails, there are de facto two\n\t\t\t// voters remaining. Only 3 can win an election (due to its log containing\n\t\t\t// all committed entries), but to do so it will need 1 to vote. But 1\n\t\t\t// considers itself a learner and will continue to do so until 3 has\n\t\t\t// stepped up as leader, replicates the conf change to 1, and 1 applies it.\n\t\t\t// Ultimately, by receiving a request to vote, the learner realizes that\n\t\t\t// the candidate believes it to be a voter, and that it should act\n\t\t\t// accordingly. The candidate's config may be stale, too; but in that case\n\t\t\t// it won't win the election, at least in the absence of the bug discussed\n\t\t\t// in:\n\t\t\t// https://github.com/etcd-io/etcd/issues/7625#issuecomment-488798263.\n\t\t\tr.logger.Infof(\"%x [logterm: %d, index: %d, vote: %x] cast %s for %x [logterm: %d, index: %d] at term %d\",\nfunc (l *raftLog) nextUnstableSnapshot() *pb.Snapshot {\n\treturn l.unstable.nextSnapshot()\n}\n\n// hasNextUnstableSnapshot returns if there is a snapshot that is available to\n// be applied to the local storage and is not already in-progress.\nfunc (l *raftLog) hasNextUnstableSnapshot() bool {\n\treturn l.unstable.nextSnapshot() != nil\n}\n\n// hasNextOrInProgressSnapshot returns if there is pending snapshot waiting for\n// applying or in the process of being applied.\nfunc (l *raftLog) hasNextOrInProgressSnapshot() bool {\n\treturn l.unstable.snapshot != nil\n}\n\nfunc (l *raftLog) snapshot() (pb.Snapshot, error) {\n\tif l.unstable.snapshot != nil {\n\t\treturn *l.unstable.snapshot, nil\n\t}\n\treturn l.storage.Snapshot()\n}\n\nfunc (l *raftLog) firstIndex() uint64 {\n\tif i, ok := l.unstable.maybeFirstIndex(); ok {\n\t\treturn i\n\t}\n\tindex, err := l.storage.FirstIndex()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tpanic(err) // TODO(bdarnell)\n\t}\n\treturn index\n}\n\nfunc (l *raftLog) lastIndex() uint64 {\n\tif i, ok := l.unstable.maybeLastIndex(); ok {\n\t\treturn i\n\t}\n\ti, err := l.storage.LastIndex()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tpanic(err) // TODO(bdarnell)\n\t}\n\treturn i\n}\n\nfunc (r *raft) restore(s pb.Snapshot) bool {\n\tif s.Metadata.Index <= r.raftLog.committed {\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\tif r.state != StateFollower {\n\t\t// This is defense-in-depth: if the leader somehow ended up applying a\n\t\t// snapshot, it could move into a new term without moving into a\n\t\t// follower state. This should never fire, but if it did, we'd have\n\t\t// prevented damage by returning early, so log only a loud warning.\n\t\t//\n\t\t// At the time of writing, the instance is guaranteed to be in follower\n\t\t// state when this method is called.\n\t\tr.logger.Warningf(\"%x attempted to restore snapshot as leader; should never happen\", r.id)\n\t\tr.becomeFollower(r.Term+1, None)\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\n\t// More defense-in-depth: throw away snapshot if recipient is not in the\n\t// config. This shouldn't ever happen (at the time of writing) but lots of\n\t// code here and there assumes that r.id is in the progress tracker.\n\tfound := false\n\tcs := s.Metadata.ConfState\n\n\tfor _, set := range [][]uint64{\n\t\tcs.Voters,\n\t\tcs.Learners,\n\t\tcs.VotersOutgoing,\n\t\t// `LearnersNext` doesn't need to be checked. According to the rules, if a peer in\n\t\t// `LearnersNext`, it has to be in `VotersOutgoing`.\n\t} {\n\t\tfor _, id := range set {\n\t\t\tif id == r.id {\n\t\t\t\tfound = true\n\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\tif found {\n\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif !found {\n\t\tr.logger.Warningf(\n\t\t\t\"%x attempted to restore snapshot but it is not in the ConfState %v; should never happen\",\n\t\t\tr.id, cs,\n\t\t)\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\n\t// Now go ahead and actually restore.\n\n\tid := entryID{term: s.Metadata.Term, index: s.Metadata.Index}\n\tif r.raftLog.matchTerm(id) {\n\t\t// TODO(pav-kv): can print %+v of the id, but it will change the format.\n\t\tlast := r.raftLog.lastEntryID()\n\t\tr.logger.Infof(\"%x [commit: %d, lastindex: %d, lastterm: %d] fast-forwarded commit to snapshot [index: %d, term: %d]\",\n\t\t\tr.id, r.raftLog.committed, last.index, last.term, id.index, id.term)\n\t\tr.raftLog.commitTo(s.Metadata.Index)\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\n\tr.raftLog.restore(s)\n\n\t// Reset the configuration and add the (potentially updated) peers in anew.\n\tr.trk = tracker.MakeProgressTracker(r.trk.MaxInflight, r.trk.MaxInflightBytes)\n\tcfg, trk, err := confchange.Restore(confchange.Changer{\n\t\tTracker:   r.trk,\n\t\tLastIndex: r.raftLog.lastIndex(),\n\t}, cs)\n\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\t// This should never happen. Either there's a bug in our config change\n\t\t// handling or the client corrupted the conf change.\n\t\tpanic(fmt.Sprintf(\"unable to restore config %+v: %s\", cs, err))\n\t}\n\n\tassertConfStatesEquivalent(r.logger, cs, r.switchToConfig(cfg, trk))\n\n\tlast := r.raftLog.lastEntryID()\n\tr.logger.Infof(\"%x [commit: %d, lastindex: %d, lastterm: %d] restored snapshot [index: %d, term: %d]\",\n\t\tr.id, r.raftLog.committed, last.index, last.term, id.index, id.term)\n\treturn true\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > build_snapshot_candidate.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nm=json.load(open('../audit-spec/v3.json'))\nnewid='F_pending_snapshot'\nedges={'B_recovery':'produces_fact_ids','B_append_response_packaging':'consumes_fact_ids','B_step_context_and_storage':'consumes_fact_ids','B_elect_transfer':'consumes_fact_ids','B_ready_application':'consumes_fact_ids'}\nfor b in m['behaviors']:\n if b['id'] in edges:b[edges[b['id']]].append(newid)\n if b['id']=='B_recovery':\n  b['writes'].append('Full restore establishes unstable.snapshot at the incoming snapshot index; an already matching log prefix takes the fast-forward branch and does not establish this pending snapshot.')\n if b['id']=='B_append_response_packaging':\n  b['reads'].append('The pending snapshot supplied in Ready; its pointer is attached to the local append completion.')\n if b['id']=='B_step_context_and_storage':\n  b['important_branches'].append('MsgStorageApplyResp only advances entry application progress and quota; it does not clear unstable.snapshot. MsgStorageAppendResp with a snapshot calls appliedSnap, whose stableSnapTo clears only the matching pending index.')\n if b['id']=='B_ready_application':\n  b['writes'].append('Ready acceptance marks a pending snapshot in progress without clearing the snapshot pointer; the pointer continues blocking new committed-entry delivery.')\n  b['source_ids']+=['S_unstable_stable','S_log_snapshot']\nm['facts'].append(dict(id=newid,meaning='The local unstable log retains a snapshot to be completed, even after Ready has handed it to local storage. Its presence is a recovery barrier consumed by campaign eligibility and committed-entry delivery. It is not evidence that snapshot IO or state-machine installation has completed.',identity={'owner':'local raft instance and unstable log','snapshot':'unstable.snapshot.Metadata.Index; payload also retains snapshot term and ConfState'},validity_context='Established only on full snapshot restore, not rejected snapshots or matching-prefix fast-forward. Ordinary role reset does not clear it. Ready acceptance marks in-progress status; a matching-index snapshot completion clears it independently of the response protocol term. A newer full restore replaces the pending object.',representation=['raftLog.unstable.snapshot','raftLog.unstable.snapshotInProgress','MsgStorageAppendResp.Snapshot'],invalidators=['B_step_context_and_storage','B_recovery'],reinterpreters=[],durability='Volatile pending-work state. Storage responses are owed only after the local append work completes. The pointer does not certify durable storage or application state.',recovery='New construction uses Storage snapshot/ConfState and HardState; pending local message objects are not restored. Incoming full snapshots establish a new pending barrier.',source_ids=['S_restore_config','S_log_decision','S_log_snapshot','S_unstable_stable','S_unstable_replace','S_append_messages','S_step','S_apply_progress','S_async_usage'],unknowns=['The asynchronous caller contract does not explicitly describe serialization of state-machine snapshot installation against an older configuration batch already handed to the apply target.']))\nfor f in m['facts']:f.pop('established_by',None);f.pop('consumed_by',None)\nfor a in m['activities']:a.pop('behavior_ids',None)\nchanges={bid:dict(impact='dependency',source_ids=['S_restore_config','S_log_snapshot','S_unstable_stable','S_unstable_replace','S_append_messages','S_step','S_apply_progress'],rationale='Expose the already traced pending-snapshot lifecycle as an explicit Fact with its producer, completion invalidator and distinct eligibility/delivery consumers.',preserves='The append-quorum and joint-read Candidates retain their existing Fact meanings, dependencies, claims and fixed observation scopes. Neither checked history contains snapshot restore. This addition makes a distinct recovery barrier navigable without changing their interpretation.') for bid in edges}\njson.dump(m,open('snapshot-support-map.json','w'),indent=2)\nq=dict(question='With a full snapshot pending on a voter using AsyncStorageWrites, can completion of older normal-entry application work allow an explicit Campaign before the snapshot append response is delivered?',importance='Campaigning before the pending recovery barrier is released could let authority acquisition use a restored log/configuration while local snapshot work remains incomplete. The selected discriminator concerns local campaign admission; an election win, conflicting decision or client-visible consequence would require independent history and observations.',disposition='needs_specific_evidence',preferred_check='controlled_schedule',participants=['Elected leader and quorum follower producing a snapshot prefix','Lagging voter receiving a full snapshot','Serialized RawNode caller and separate FIFO append/apply workers'],objects=['Pending snapshot identity','Previously issued normal-entry apply batch and attached response','Campaign request','Term, role and outbound vote requests'],contexts=['Three fixed voters with all bootstrap configuration entries applied','AsyncStorageWrites and no pre-vote; explicit Campaign, without election timer assumptions','Snapshot produced from an actually committed and applied leader prefix after the receiving voter is isolated','Older apply batch contains only normal entries; complete it before state-machine snapshot installation','No restart, configuration transition or critical raft-state assignment'],event_paths=['Proposal and replication -> leader application -> MemoryStorage.CreateSnapshot and Compact -> automatic snapshot fallback -> follower full restore','Earlier MsgStorageApply work -> apply normal entries -> attached MsgStorageApplyResp -> explicit Campaign while snapshot append work remains held','Complete snapshot storage and installation -> attached MsgStorageAppendResp -> repeat Campaign with a fixed output drain'],activity_classes=['A2','A3','A5','A6'],behavior_ids=list(edges),fact_ids=[newid],supporting_behavior_ids={'B_propose_replicate':'Actual missing-predecessor replication path produces MsgSnap from leader storage.','B_aggregate_commit':'Quorum commitment establishes the producer prefix from which the application creates the snapshot.'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['promotable directly tests hasNextOrInProgressSnapshot, while MsgStorageApplyResp only changes applied progress; source review predicts the barrier remains intact.','Ready acceptance changes snapshotInProgress but leaves the pointer used by the guard present.','Snapshot fast-forward when its index/term already matches the recipient log does not create the selected pending barrier and must be distinguished in construction.'],unknowns=['Establish a producer-derived full-restore history with a genuine earlier normal-entry apply batch still outstanding.','Determine the applicable local campaign responsibility and independent observations without treating Campaign return nil as election admission.','Broader snapshot/state-machine ordering remains unresolved for older configuration batches; that case is excluded from this discriminator.'],trigger_rationale='The prior source handoff separated applied-index advancement from snapshot completion. A single actual pending snapshot with an older normal apply response isolates the consumer guard with fewer caller-contract assumptions than overlapping configuration application or replacement snapshots. Compare term/role/vote output for Campaign while held and after completed snapshot work; controls should finish under a fixed schedule rather than await an election win.')\nids=set()\nfor b in m['behaviors']:\n if b['id'] in q['behavior_ids'] or b['id'] in q['supporting_behavior_ids']:ids.update(b['source_ids'])\nids.update(m['facts'][-1]['source_ids']);ids.update(['S_memory_snapshot','S_transfer_snapshot_test','S_ready_usage'])\nq['source_ids']=sorted(ids)\ns=dict(action='continue',rationale='Map the distinct recovery barrier and select a bounded authority-admission question. Preserve the unresolved cross-target state-machine configuration contract as a limitation instead of inventing an obligation.',map_path='snapshot-support-map.json',map_changes=changes,question=q,feedback=dict(ref_ids=['S_async_usage','S_restore_config','S_log_snapshot','S_step','S_apply_progress','S_memory_snapshot','S_transfer_snapshot_test'],answered='The pending snapshot pointer, not applied index or snapshotInProgress alone, is the shared object linking full recovery to campaign admission and next committed-entry delivery. Full restore produces it, Ready retains it in progress, ordinary apply responses do not clear it, and matching-index snapshot completion retires it. The new map records these distinct direct edges under their existing activity ownership. The transfer test supplies an adjacent expectation, not execution of this question.',remaining=['Construct the actual full-restore prefix and older normal application batch through public RawNode and storage APIs.','Fix the local duty and an independent Campaign-admission oracle before formal execution.'],understanding='updated',rationale='The current code guard is concrete counterevidence to premature admission. A controlled public-entry history can discriminate whether that guard survives real asynchronous handoffs, while avoiding the unsettled configuration/application ordering branch.'))\njson.dump(s,open('submission-snapshot-candidate.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\npython3 build_snapshot_candidate.py\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_19-39-39-etcd_raft-real-run --submission submission-snapshot-candidate.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
